Where and when: read on 2026-10-12:

  https://rapidmapping.emergency.copernicus.eu/backend/dashboard-api/public-activations/?code=EMSR773
  (the activation's record, which lists the product and its image)
  https://rapidmapping.emergency.copernicus.eu/backend/EMSR773/AOI03/GRA_PRODUCT/EMSR773_AOI03_GRA_PRODUCT_v2.zip
  (70,968,988 bytes, SHA-256 8248feef4f0a9938dfaff103a6e3d6960294f4572d193df919eda55ad79880ba;
  the layers EMSR773_AOI03_GRA_PRODUCT_observedEventA_v2.json,
  EMSR773_AOI03_GRA_PRODUCT_builtUpP_v2.json and
  EMSR773_AOI03_GRA_PRODUCT_areaOfInterestA_v2.json inside it)

Kept, and what was changed: of the observed flood, each patch's class,
"Flooded area" named "Standing water" and "Flood trace" named "Flood
traces", and its area, given in hectares and turned into km²; of the
graded buildings, each point's grade, its kind ("11-Residential
Buildings" as Residential, "12-Non-residential Buildings" as
Non-residential, the rest as Unclassified) and its name where the map
gives one; of the area of interest, its outline, with its area measured
on the ellipsoid. Left out: the product's other layers (facilities,
transport, image footprints) and every other attribute. Every geometry is
as delivered, in longitude and latitude. This is a modified version of
the data. A patch of 0.4 km² in the west of the area, which the image did
not cover, was not analysed by the service.


Overture Maps divisions
-----------------------

Dataset: towns (the 24 municipalities the area of interest takes in, as
outlines)

Publisher: the Overture Maps Foundation, its divisions theme
(division_area), release 2026-09-23.1, whose outlines and names here all
come from OpenStreetMap.
https://docs.overturemaps.org/attribution/

Licence: Open Database License 1.0 (ODbL-1.0), the divisions theme's
licence, as Overture's attribution page states it ("License for theme:
ODbL © OpenStreetMap contributors"). The ODbL applies to this dataset as
a derived database: anyone may use it, and a public derived database
must be offered under the ODbL as well.

Credit: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Overture Maps Foundation.

Where and when: read on 2026-10-12 from Overture's public bucket, the
localities in Spain whose bounding box meets the area of interest:

  s3://overturemaps-us-west-2/release/2026-09-23.1/theme=divisions/type=division_area/*.parquet

Kept: each municipality's id, primary name and outline. Left out: the
comarcas, which Overture also files as localities but which each hold
several municipalities (the comarca of València, with the city's own
outline, gives way to the city), and every other property. This is a
modified version of the data.


